ustom-gesture-recognizers"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/uigesturerecognizer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to your map programmatically or via storyboard. Adding custom responses to gesture recognizers can enhance your user’s experience, but try to use standard gestures where possible.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The gesture recognizers that you add will take priority over the built-in gesture recognizer. You can also set up your own gesture recognizer to work simultaneously with built-in gesture recognizers by using ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/uigesturerecognizerdelegate\/1624208-gesturerecognizer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", allowing you to enhance already existing gesture recognizers.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also add gesture recognizers that are only called when the default gesture recognizer fails (and vice versa), such as when a user taps on a part of the map that is not an annotation. The documentation for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" includes an example of how to create a fallback gesture recognizer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you would like to disable a specific set of gesture recognizers, such as zoom, you can set the Boolean value for the appropriate property to ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can then add your own gesture recognizers to perform those actions.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"User Interactions"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"variants":